## Thorough Investigation: Sketchpad Scene Architecture & FlattenDesign Issue

Based on my analysis of the codebase, here's a complete breakdown of the architecture:

---

### 1. **Scene Building Architecture - [compose/sketchpad/index.tsx](compose/sketchpad/index.tsx)**

#### Blob URL Creation & Caching

**Lines [7575-7620](compose/sketchpad/index.tsx#L7575-L7620):** `CollaborativeKitStore.getFileBlobUrl()`
```typescript
async getFileBlobUrl(guid: string): Promise<string | null> {
  const kit = this._kitStore.getSnapshot().kit;
  const fileState = getOrCreateKitFileState(this._kitStore);

  // 1. Check object URL cache
  const cachedBlobUrl = fileState.objectUrls.get(guid);
  if (cachedBlobUrl) return cachedBlobUrl;

  // 2. Check blob cache
  const cachedBlob = fileState.blobs.get(guid);
  if (cachedBlob) return createKitFileObjectUrl(this._kitStore, guid, cachedBlob);

  // 3. Find file in kit
  const file = kit.files?.find((existingFile) => existingFile.guid === guid);
  if (!file) return null;

  // 4. Try binary store (local readFile)
  const binaryStore = this._kitStore as KitBinaryStore;
  if (typeof binaryStore.readFile === "function") {
    try {
      const blob = await binaryStore.readFile(storagePath);
      if (blob) {
        fileState.blobs.set(guid, blob);
        return createKitFileObjectUrl(this._kitStore, guid, blob);
      }
    } catch (error) {}
  }

  // 5. Try provider (network download)
  const provider = await getKitFileProvider(this._kitStore, kit.guid);
  if (provider) {
    try {
      const blob = await provider.download(kit.guid, file.guid, storagePath);
      fileState.blobs.set(guid, blob);
      return createKitFileObjectUrl(this._kitStore, guid, blob);
    } catch (error) {}
  }

  // 6. Try readable remote URL
  const readableUrl = getReadableKitFileUrl(fileState, file);
  if (readableUrl) {
    const blob = await fetchReadableKitFileBlob(readableUrl);
    // ... continues
  }
}
```
**Key Strategy:** Three-tier caching: objectUrls → blobs → file load

---

#### CollaborativeKitStore Cache in SketchpadStore

**Lines [19459](compose/sketchpad/index.tsx#L19459-L19459):** Cache declaration:
```typescript
private readonly collaborativeKitStoreCache: Map<string, CollaborativeKitStore> = new Map();
```

**Lines [20377-20381](compose/sketchpad/index.tsx#L20377-L20381):** Cache usage in `kit()` method:
```typescript
kit(guid: string): CollaborativeKitStore {
  const kitStore = this.kits.get(guid);
  if (!kitStore) {
    throw new Error(`Kit with guid ${guid} not found`);
  }
  let cached = this.collaborativeKitStoreCache.get(guid);
  if (!cached || cached.store !== kitStore) {
    cached = new CollaborativeKitStore(kitStore);
    this.collaborativeKitStoreCache.set(guid, cached);
  }
  return cached;
}
```
**Purpose:** Ensures stable CollaborativeKitStore instance per kit guid. Fixes React's `useSyncExternalStore` re-subscription issues.

**Lines [19995](compose/sketchpad/index.tsx#L19995):** Cache cleanup on kit deletion:
```typescript
private readonly collaborativeKitStoreCache.delete(guid);
```

---

#### PieceMesh - Three.js Model Loading via Blob URL

**Lines [37920-37950](compose/sketchpad/index.tsx#L37920-L37950):** Blob URL retrieval and fallback rendering:
```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  if (!fileGuid) {
    setBlobUrl(null);
    return;
  }
  let cancelled = false;
  let currentBlobUrl: string | null = null;
  (async () => {
    try {
      const url = await kitStore.getFileBlobUrl(fileGuid);
      if (!cancelled && url) {
        currentBlobUrl = url;
        setBlobUrl(url);  // ✅ Set for three.js loader
      } else if (!cancelled && !url) {
        console.warn("[PieceMesh] No URL available for file:", fileGuid);
      }
    } catch (error) {
      console.error("[PieceMesh] Failed to get blob URL:", error);
    }
  })();

  return () => {
    cancelled = true;  // Cancel if component unmounts
  };
}, [fileGuid, kitStore]);
```

**Lines [40670-40730](compose/sketchpad/index.tsx#L40670-L40730):** Three.js model loading with blob URLs:
```typescript
const gltf = useGLTF(url);  // Load GLTF/GLB models

const scene = useFBX(url);  // Load FBX models
```

**What happens:** 
1. Blob URL passed to `useGLTF()` or `useFBX()` 
2. Three.js loaders parse the blob URL
3. If blob URL is null: renders fallback box geometry
4. Cancel flag prevents race conditions on unmount

